- page_title << "DNS Check"
- page_title << @domain.name

.pageContent.pageContent--compact
  %h2.pageContent__title DNS Setup for #{@domain.name}
  %p.pageContent__intro.u-margin
    Follow the instructions below to configure DNS records for
    %b= @domain.name
    and verify everything is set up correctly.

  - unless @domain.verified?
    .u-margin
      %h3.pageContent__subTitle Domain Verification
      %p.pageContent__text
        Before configuring DNS records, you need to verify ownership of this domain
        by adding a TXT record with the following value:

      %pre.codeBlock.u-margin= @domain.dns_verification_string

      %p.pageContent__text
        Once you've added this record, click the button below to verify.

      .buttonSet.u-margin
        = link_to "Verify TXT record", public_domain_check_verify_path(@domain.public_token), method: :post, class: "button"

  - if @domain.verified?
    .u-margin
      %p.pageContent__text.u-green.u-bold
        %span.label.label--green Verified
        Domain ownership has been verified.

    .u-margin.buttonSet
      = link_to "Check my records are correct", public_domain_check_dns_path(@domain.public_token), method: :post, class: "button"
    - if @domain.dns_checked_at
      %p.u-margin DNS records were last checked #{distance_of_time_in_words_to_now @domain.dns_checked_at} ago.

    %h3.pageContent__subTitle SPF Record
    - if @domain.spf_status == 'OK'
      %p.pageContent__text.u-green.u-bold
        %span.label.label--green Good
        Your SPF record looks good!
    - elsif !@domain.spf_status.nil?
      %p.pageContent__text.u-orange.u-bold
        %span.label.label--orange Warning
        = @domain.spf_error

    %p.pageContent__text
      You need to add a TXT record at the apex/root of your domain (@) with the following
      content. If you already send mail from another service, you may just need to add
      <b>include:#{Postal::Config.dns.spf_include}</b> to your existing record.
    %pre.codeBlock.u-margin= @domain.spf_record

    %h3.pageContent__subTitle DKIM Record
    - if @domain.dkim_status == 'OK'
      %p.pageContent__text.u-green.u-bold
        %span.label.label--green Good
        Your DKIM record looks good!
    - elsif !@domain.dkim_status.nil?
      %p.pageContent__text.u-orange.u-bold
        %span.label.label--orange Warning
        = @domain.dkim_error

    %p.pageContent__text
      You need to add a new TXT record with the name <b>#{@domain.dkim_record_name}</b>
      with the following content.
    %pre.codeBlock.u-margin= @domain.dkim_record

    %h3.pageContent__subTitle Return Path
    - if @domain.return_path_status == 'OK'
      %p.pageContent__text.u-green.u-bold
        %span.label.label--green Good
        Your return path looks good.
    - elsif @domain.return_path_status == 'Missing'
      %p.pageContent__text.u-grey.u-bold
        %span.label.label--grey OK
        There's no return path for this domain. This is OK but we recommend adding the record to improve deliverability.
    - elsif !@domain.return_path_status.nil?
      %p.pageContent__text.u-orange.u-bold
        %span.label.label--orange Warning
        = @domain.return_path_error

    %p.pageContent__text
      This is optional but recommended. Add a <b>CNAME</b> record at
      <b>#{@domain.return_path_domain}</b> pointing to:
    %pre.codeBlock.u-margin= Postal::Config.dns.return_path_domain

    %h3.pageContent__subTitle MX Records
    - if @domain.mx_status == 'OK'
      %p.pageContent__text.u-green.u-bold
        %span.label.label--green Good
        Your MX records look good!
    - elsif @domain.mx_status == 'Missing'
      %p.pageContent__text.u-grey.u-bold
        %span.label.label--grey OK
        No MX records point to us. Incoming mail won't be received.
    - elsif !@domain.mx_status.nil?
      %p.pageContent__text.u-orange.u-bold
        %span.label.label--orange Warning
        = @domain.mx_error

    %p.pageContent__text
      If you wish to receive incoming e-mail, add the following MX records with priority <b>10</b>.
    %pre.codeBlock.u-margin= Postal::Config.dns.mx_records.join("\n")
